{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/j7wvge","slide":1,"text":"Architecture verified against nets/audioset_crnn.py and current run.sh configuration. Front end: datasets/audioset_logmel_dataset.py and README.md. Default channels [32,64,96], 2-layer bidirectional GRU with hidden size 128 per direction, embedding dimension 128, dropout 0.2. CNN tensors [B,1,T,64] -> [B,32,T,32] -> [B,64,T,16] -> [B,96,T,8]. Frequency mean yields [B,96,T], then transpose [B,T,96]. Packed sequences use valid lengths. Frame logits have shape [B,T]; sigmoid yields conditional probabilities. frame_mask excludes batch padding. Training uses real strong annotations and masked balanced BCE, omitted from this forward architecture diagram. Class conditions are single-class one-hot vectors, not multi-hot vectors. B=batch size, T=number of frames. Reference image used for black/white/gray layout and module expansion style only."}